WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
In this video, I'll be introducing the concept of subsets and supersets

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:09.300
The dots on the board here represent elements of a set.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.380
The lines represent the sets themselves.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:16.480
These lines have been labeled B, A and U

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:25.680
We can say that B is a subset of A because B contains...because all elements of B are elements of A

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.400
We can also say that B is a proper subset of A because all elements of B are elements of A

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.400
and there are elements of A that are not within the set B.

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:49.640
We can also say that the set A is a superset of the set B because A contains all of the elements of B.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
And being even more specific, we can say that A is a proper superset of B because A contains all elements of B

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.360
and there are elements of A that are not elements of B.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:08.920
What we cannot say is that U is a proper subset of A.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:17.400
Although the circle here is bigger than A, it just takes up more space, it doesn't contain any more elements

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.000
So all the elements...so U contains all elements of A

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:25.400
however, U does not contain any extra elements.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.900
So U is a subset of A, and A is actually a subset of U

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.160
U is a superset of A, and A is also a superset of U

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:37.960
So the sets A and U in this case are actually equal.

